# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

From positions to exposures, concentration, return-based risk, stress scenarios, and limit checks.
It runs as generated, and it is yours to change.

```bash
uv sync
uv run {{ project_name }} report     # a demo report, in reports/
uv run {{ project_name }} check      # every limit; exits 1 on a breach, so a scheduler can alert
uv run {{ project_name }} sections   # what you can put in the report
```

## Use your book

Point `config.toml` at your files. Positions are weights of NAV, with shorts negative:

```text
date,AAPL,MSFT,XOM
2024-03-28,0.05,-0.03,0.02
```

`prices` has the same shape, and turns on volatility, value at risk, risk contributors, and beta.
`groups` is a CSV with the columns `asset,group`, for sector or any other grouping.

## Make it yours

| Level | What you do | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Set data, limits, and stress scenarios | `config.toml` |
| 2 | Choose the report's sections | `sections` in `config.toml` |
| 3 | Add your own checks, sections, and file formats | `{{ package_name }}/firm/` |
| 4 | Change anything else; you own the code | Everywhere, with the tests to catch mistakes |

`AGENTS.md` tells a coding assistant the same rules. See `LIMITATIONS.md` for what this does not do.
